Run from the kernel tree:
  CC=clang python3 tools/testing/selftests/sparklink/run_security_remediation.py

Requires Rust with the current kernel-supported syntax and a C compiler with
ASan/UBSan runtimes. LeakSanitizer requires an environment without ptrace.
Missing tools/runtimes or failed assertions fail the test; there is no fallback
PASS or skipped assertion. No production fault switches are introduced.

The runner copies the unchanged retained kernel crypto source and exact archived security model to a private
build directory, appends child tests for private state, and links controllable FFI
dependencies. It compiles the exact production C CTR function against counted
allocation/crypto dependencies. These verify errno propagation, fail-closed legacy
pairing, KDF commit, counter overflow and failure commit of data/IV/address. They
are not real crypto algorithms, standard vectors, peer interoperability or RF.

Pairing is deliberately unavailable pending authenticated per-connection state.
Unpublished legacy test ioctl numbers still exist for caller migration, but their
production handlers return EOPNOTSUPP. Tests call retained actual wrappers instead. Model tests are historical; the default runtime has no SecurityInner/RpaManager.
The real WS73 Native discovery implementation is untouched and needs regression
on each new kernel in a VM with real devices before hardware preservation claims.

SDK111 security event envelope proof (CBMC 6.11.0):
  cbmc tools/testing/selftests/sparklink/security/relay_envelope_cbmc.c \
    --function main --unwind 266 --unwinding-assertions --bounds-check \
    --pointer-check --signed-overflow-check --unsigned-overflow-check \
    --conversion-check --trace

The harness includes the actual driver dli.c. Packets are nondeterministic,
0..265 bytes, dynamically allocated at the advertised input size; allocation
failure is not excluded. All header/status/handle/index/payload bytes are free.
Properties cover recognition, exact nested lengths and memory/arithmetic safety.
No alignment/padding from the reference Host's C structures is assumed. The
scope does not cover framing above 265 bytes, RF, command serialization,
generation/lifetime attribution, key validation, or security state transitions.
Record the exact source/harness hashes, command, tool version and terminal result
for each run. Timeout, missing tools, unsupported or incomplete unwinding are
NOT_PROVEN, never a hardware or pairing PASS.
